<title>SOUTH AFRICA: CRICKET-TRANSVAAL SET 408 TO BEAT NATAL.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-TRANSVAAL SET 408 TO BEAT NATAL.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-02-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Transvaal were set a</p>
<p>formidable target of 408 for victory by Natal in their four-day</p>
<p>Supersport Series match in Johannesburg on Sunday.</p>
<p>Natal declared their second innings closed at 241 for eight</p>
<p>after opting not to enforce the follow-on after claiming a</p>
<p>166-run first innings lead. At the close Transvaal had moved to</p>
<p>four without loss.</p>
<p>Needing to make 258 to avoid the follow-on Transvaal were</p>
<p>bowled out for 241 as overnight batsman Ken Rutherford could add</p>
<p>only one to his 87 and the Transvaal tail subsided.</p>
<p>Natal opted to give their test attack a rest and batted a</p>
<p>second time with Andrew Hudson making 49 and Jonty Rhodes 43 in</p>
<p>an innings which failed to spark to life.</p>
<p>Natal took their overall lead beyond 400 before declaring to</p>
<p>leave Transvaal a minimum of 108 overs to reach their target.</p>
